---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="LoanSlam | Fail-closed AI for regulated lending conversations"
  description="LoanSlam is a prototype conversation engine that keeps model output behind retrieval, validation, and trace evidence."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Regulated lending support, without blind model trust</p>
        <h1>LoanSlam</h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">
          A fail-closed AI conversation engine where the model proposes each turn and deterministic
          code decides what can safely reach the user.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/platform/">See the platform</a>
          <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/evidence/">Review the evidence model</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <img
        class="hero-visual"
        src="/trace-console.svg"
        alt="A LoanSlam trace console showing planner, validator, and audit states"
        width="720"
        height="520"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--panel">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">The operating promise</p>
      <div class="claim-row">
        <h2>Useful AI is allowed to help. It is never allowed to be the boundary.</h2>
        <p>
          LoanSlam separates fluent drafting from final authority. The planner can interpret intent,
          ask for clarification, and compose a candidate response. The validator enforces policy,
          grounding, sensitive-data limits, and handoff rules before anything is shown.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid grid--3">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card-kicker">Planner</span>
        <h2>Model proposals stay untrusted.</h2>
        <p>
          The LLM returns a structured plan with route, answer shape, and safety flags. It does not
          get the final say.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card-kicker">Validator</span>
        <h2>Policy checks run in code.</h2>
        <p>
          Unsupported answers, excluded topics, and account-specific requests are blocked or routed
          to the right human fallback.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card-kicker">Evidence</span>
        <h2>Every turn can be inspected.</h2>
        <p>
          Trace artifacts keep proposals, retrieval, rule decisions, and final responses together
          for review.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built for careful rollout</p>
        <h2>Prototype first. Synthetic data first. Human review first.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="check-list">
        <p><strong>No live applications.</strong> The current site is a product surface, not a lending flow.</p>
        <p><strong>No production personal data.</strong> Demo runs are synthetic and inspectable.</p>
        <p><strong>No hidden automation.</strong> The system earns trust through route evidence and traces.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
